### Gateway API Test Requests

# Variables
@gateway_url = https://localhost:5000
@identity_url = https://localhost:5001

### Health Check (Public)
GET {{gateway_url}}/health

### Login to get JWT token (Public)
POST {{gateway_url}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### Test protected endpoint in Identity service (requires token)
# Note: Gateway will add X-User-Id header when forwarding this request
GET {{gateway_url}}/api/auth/test-protected
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### Public catalog endpoint (no authentication required)
# Note: No X-User-Id header will be added for public routes
GET {{gateway_url}}/api/catalog/products

### Protected catalog endpoint (requires token)
# Note: Gateway will add X-User-Id header when forwarding this request
GET {{gateway_url}}/api/catalog/admin/products
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### Protected orders endpoint (requires token)
# Note: Gateway will add X-User-Id header when forwarding this request
# The orders service can use Request.Headers["X-User-Id"] to get the user ID
GET {{gateway_url}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### Protected users endpoint (requires token)
# Note: Gateway will add X-User-Id header when forwarding this request
GET {{gateway_url}}/api/users/profile
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### Public API endpoint (no authentication required)
# Note: No X-User-Id header will be added for public routes
GET {{gateway_url}}/api/public/status

### Test invalid token (should return 401)
GET {{gateway_url}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer invalid_token

### Test missing token (should return 401)
GET {{gateway_url}}/api/orders

### Test malformed authorization header (should return 401)
GET {{gateway_url}}/api/orders
Authorization: InvalidScheme token_here

###